\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Can every nonsingular equation $w\in\Gamma*F_n$ with coefficients in a group $\Gamma$ be solved over $\Gamma$? Also, for every nontrivial word $w\in F_2$, does there exist $n_0$ such that the word map $w:\operatorname{PU}(n)\times\operatorname{PU}(n)\to\operatorname{PU}(n)$ is surjective for every $n\geq n_0$?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2014/42}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Can every nonsingular equation $w\in\Gamma*F_n$ with coefficients in a group $\Gamma$ be solved over $\Gamma$? Also, for every nontrivial word $w\in F_2$, does there exist $n_0$ such that the word map $w:\operatorname{PU}(n)\times\operatorname{PU}(n)\to\operatorname{PU}(n)$ is surjective for every $n\geq n_0$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 30002675 (OWR-13112-001). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
